hadiths[29]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2094","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` one day Jibreel (peace be upon him) was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when a loud sound of a door opening was heard. He raised his head and Jibreel (peace be upon him) said, ""This is a door of the heaven which has opened today, and it has never opened before today."" Then an angel descended from it. And Jibreel (peace be upon him) said, ""This angel who has descended to the earth has never descended except on this day."" He greeted (the Prophet) and said, ""Receive the glad tidings of two lights which have been given to you, which no prophet before you was given: one is Surah Al-Fatihah and the other is the concluding verses of Surah Al-Baqarah. You will not recite a single letter from them except that you will be granted what you ask for."""
"2095","´Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Bahili رضي الله عنه says that` I heard the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم say, ""Recite the Qur'an, for it will come as an intercessor for its reciters on the Day of Resurrection. And recite the two shining Surahs, which are Surah Al-Baqarah and Surah Aal-e-Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they are two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading for those who recite them. And taking recourse to Surah Al-Baqarah is a blessing, and leaving it is a cause of regret, and the magicians cannot confront it."" Muawiyah said that the word ""batala"" in the hadith means magician."
"2096","Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Abu'l-Mundhir! Which verse in Allah's Book is the greatest with you?"" I replied, ""Allah and His Messenger (peace be upon him) know best."" He (peace be upon him) said, ""O Abu'l-Mundhir! Which verse in Allah's Book is the greatest with you?"" I replied, ""(Allah! There is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of [all] existence)"" (i.e., Ayat al-Kursi). So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) struck my chest (happily) with his hand and said, ""O Abu'l-Mundhir! May knowledge be blessed for you."""
"2097","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever recites the last two verses of Surah Al-Baqarah at night, they will suffice him for the night."
"2098","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever memorizes the first ten verses of Surah Al-Kahf will be protected from the trial of the Dajjal. In another narration, it is mentioned that (by memorizing) the last verses of Surah Al-Kahf, one will be granted refuge from the Dajjal."
"2099","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Is any one of you incapable of reciting one third of the Qur'an every night?"" The companions asked, ""How can anyone recite one third of the Qur'an?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Surah Al-Ikhlas (Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad) is equal to one third of the Qur'an."""
"2100","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a man as the commander of a troop, and he used to recite the Qur'an in the prayer of his troop and would always end his recitation with (Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad). When the troop returned, the people mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said, ""Ask him why he does so."" The companions asked him, and he replied, ""This is an attribute of the Most Merciful, and I love to recite it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Tell him that Allah loves him."""
"2101","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do you not see that tonight such verses have been revealed the like of which have never been seen before, and they are: (Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak) and (Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind)."
"2102","‘It is narrated from ‘Amir bin Wathilah that Nafi‘ bin ‘Abd al-Harith met Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) at (the place of) ‘Usfan, and Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had appointed him as the governor/collector over Makkah. Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, “Whom have you appointed as governor over the people of the wilderness?” He replied, “Ibn Abza.” Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Who is Ibn Abza?” He replied, “One of our freed slaves.” Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “You have appointed a slave over them as governor?” He replied, “He is a reciter of the Book of Allah and well-versed in the knowledge of inheritance (i.e., the laws of inheritance which the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has declared to be half of knowledge).” Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Listen! Your Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has said that Allah, because of this Book, will raise some people and will lower others.”"
"2103","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out while we were in the Suffah. He (peace be upon him) said: ""Which one of you would like to go out every morning to Bathan or Aqeeq (these were two markets of Madinah) and bring back two large-humped she-camels from there, without committing any sin and without severing the ties of kinship?"" We said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We would all like that."" He (peace be upon him) said: ""Then why does not one of you go to the mosque and learn or recite two verses from the Book of Allah? That is better for him than two she-camels, and three verses are better than three she-camels, and four are better than four she-camels, and so on, according to the number of verses, each is better than that many she-camels."""
"2104","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari رضي الله عنه narrates that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: The example of a believer who recites the Qur'an is like that of a citron, whose fragrance is pleasant and whose taste is good. And the example of a believer who does not recite the Qur'an is like that of a date, which has no fragrance but its taste is sweet. And the example of a hypocrite who recites the Qur'an is like that of a flower, whose fragrance is good but its taste is bitter. And the example of a hypocrite who does not recite the Qur'an is like that of the colocynth (bitter apple), which has no fragrance and its taste is bitter."
"2105","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The expert with the Qur'an (this may refer to a Hafiz who also acts upon it) is with the noble angels who write near the Preserved Tablet, and the one who recites the Qur'an and stumbles in it, and it is difficult for him, for him there is a double reward."
"2106","Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a man was reciting Surah Al-Kahf and nearby, a horse was tied with two long ropes. Then a cloud came over him, which began to circle and draw near, and seeing this, his horse started to shy away. When morning came, the man went to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned what had happened during the night. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “That was tranquility (sakinah) which descended due to the blessing of the Qur’an.”"
"2107","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Usaid bin Hudair (may Allah be pleased with him) was reciting the Qur'an one night in the place where he dried his dates, when his horse began to jump, and as he recited, the horse would jump. Then he started reciting again, and the horse jumped again. He said, ""I feared that (my son) Yahya might be trampled, so I went and stood by him. And what did I see but a canopy above my head, in which there were lights like lamps, and it ascended upwards until it disappeared from sight. Then I did not see it again. In the morning, I went to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and submitted, 'O Messenger of Allah! Last night I was reciting the Qur'an in my enclosure when suddenly my horse began to jump.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Recite, O son of Hudair!' He said, 'I continued reciting, and the horse jumped again.' Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Recite, O son of Hudair!' He said, 'I continued reciting, and the horse kept jumping as before.' Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Recite, O son of Hudair!' He said, 'When I finished and Yahya was near the horse, I feared that Yahya might be trampled, so I saw a canopy in which there were lights like lamps, and it ascended upwards until it was out of sight.' Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Those were angels who were listening to your recitation, and if you had continued reciting, the morning would have come and people would have seen them (the angels), and they would not have remained hidden from their sight.'"""
"2108","Sayyiduna Salim narrates from his father Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that he said: ""Envy is not permissible except for two men: one to whom Allah has given the Qur'an and he recites it day and night (and acts upon it); the other is the one to whom Allah has given wealth and he spends it (in the way of Allah) day and night."""
"2109","`Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) said that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The example of the one who memorizes the Qur'an is like that of a camel whose leg is tied; if its owner takes care of it, it remains (with him), but if he lets it go, it runs away."
"2110","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The worst among you is the one who says, ""I have forgotten such and such verse."" Rather, he should say, ""I have been made to forget."" And take care of the Qur'an and remember it, for it escapes from people's hearts faster than a tied camel is released."
"2111","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: Allah does not listen to anything as attentively as He listens to a prophet with a beautiful voice who recites the Qur'an aloud in a melodious tone."
"2112","Abu Burdah narrates from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you had seen me when I was listening to your recitation last night (you would have been very pleased). Indeed, you have been given one of the voices from the voices of the family of Dawud."
"2113","Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Qurrah says: I heard Abdullah bin Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him) say that in the year Makkah was conquered, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited Surah Al-Fath on his mount during the journey, and in his recitation he would modulate his voice. Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If I did not fear that people would crowd around me, I would have recited to you the recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"2114","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person reciting the Qur'an at night and said: May Allah have mercy on him, he reminded me of such-and-such verse which I used to leave out from such-and-such Surah."
"2115","Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard Hisham bin Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) reciting Surah Al-Furqan in a way different from the way the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had taught me. I was about to seize him quickly, but I gave him respite until he finished reciting. Then I took his cloak, put it around his neck, and dragged him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I heard him reciting Surah Al-Furqan in a manner different from the way you taught me."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Let him go,"" and told him, ""Recite."" He recited as I had heard him before, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""This Surah was revealed in this way."" Then he said to me, ""Recite."" So I recited (in the way the Messenger of Allah had taught me), and he also said, ""It was revealed in this way."" And he said, ""The Qur'an has been revealed in seven modes, so recite in whichever is easy for you."""
"2116","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) that (and he is the leader of all the reciters) Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has commanded me to recite before you the Surah (Lam Yakunilladhina Kafaru....). He (Ubayy) asked, ""Did Allah, Glorified and Exalted, mention my name?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""Yes (Allah mentioned your name before me)."" So Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) began to weep (out of joy)."
"2117","‘Aamir al-Sha’bi says that I asked Alqamah, “Was Abdullah ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the Night of the Jinn?” He said, “I asked Abdullah ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him), ‘Was any of you with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the Night of the Jinn?’ (That is, the night when the Prophet met the jinn.) He said, ‘No, but one day we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and then he was lost from us. So we searched for him in the valleys and mountain passes, but we could not find him. We thought that the jinn had taken him away or that someone had secretly killed him, and we spent the night in the worst state. When morning came, we saw that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was coming from the direction of Hira (Jabal al-Noor, a mountain between Makkah and Mina). We said, “O Messenger of Allah! Last night we lost you, and when we could not find you despite searching, we spent the night in a very bad state (without you).” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “A caller from among the jinn came to me, so I went with him and recited the Qur’an to the jinn.” Then he took us with him and showed us their traces and the traces of their fires. The jinn asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for provisions, so he said, “Every bone of an animal over which the name of Allah has been mentioned, when it falls into your hands, will be full of meat for you, and every dung of a camel will be food for your animals.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Do not use bones and dung for istinja (cleaning), for they are the food of your brothers among the jinn (and their animals).”"
"2118","Ma'n says that I heard from my father, he said: I asked Masruq, ""On the night when the jinn came and listened to the Qur'an, who informed the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) about this?"" He said: Your father (i.e., Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated to me that the Prophet (peace be upon him) was informed of the coming of the jinn by a tree."
"2119","´Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, ""Recite the Qur'an to me."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Shall I recite the Qur'an to you, while it has been revealed to you?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""I desire to hear it from someone else."" Then I recited Surah An-Nisa, until when I reached this verse ((Fakayfa idha ji'na)) (An-Nisa: 41), I raised my head or someone nudged me so I raised my head and saw that the tears were flowing from the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2120","´Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` I was in Homs when people asked me to recite the Qur'an to them. I recited Surah Yusuf. A person said, ""By Allah! It was not revealed like this."" I said, ""Woe to you! By Allah! I recited this Surah before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said, 'You have recited well.'"" In short, while I was talking to him, I smelled alcohol from him. I said, ""You drink alcohol and deny the Book of Allah? You will not leave until I administer the prescribed punishment to you."" Then I flogged him (with the prescribed lashes for drinking alcohol)."
"2121","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` one day I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) early in the morning. He (peace be upon him) heard the voices of two men who were arguing about a verse, so he (peace be upon him) came out and anger was apparent on his face. He (peace be upon him) said: The people before you were destroyed because of disputing about the Book of Allah (which is when done out of selfishness, corruption, or to mislead people. But investigating the meaning and deriving religious rulings is correct. [Nawawi])."
"2122","Narrated by Sayyiduna Jundub bin Abdullah Bajali (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite the Qur'an as long as your hearts are in agreement with your tongues, and when there is a difference between your hearts and your tongues, then get up (stop reciting)."
